## Case
AWPTCM-T27887. No steps in ck.db. Precondition: "vlan-based QinQ and vlan translation should not be
used on the same port If both vlan-based QinQ and vlan translation are applied on the same port, the
outer vlan tag will be used for translation". It tests VLAN-based QinQ, the global per-VLAN mapping
`vlan-stacking vlan <inner> outer-vlan <outer>` ("cannot be applied per interface", T27895/T27989).

This run's ask (supplementary, not the case's feature): exercise the two per-port IE520 commands that
had never been configured or put under traffic, forward and reverse:
 (A) `switchport vlan translation vlan <wire> vlan <vid> outer-vlan <outer>`, in both argument orders;
 (B) `switchport vlan translation default outer-vlan <vid>`;
plus a re-measure of the O-2 form `switchport vlan translation vlan <wire> outer-vlan <outer>`.
The question for each: does the customer C-tag survive INSIDE the outer tag (true Q-in-Q), or is it
dropped (O-2)?

