## Readings
1. Combined entry (A), both argument orders (one stored entry `vlan 2100 vlan 3997 outer-vlan 3995`):
   - Forward (customer 2100 -> provider): the frame leaves with ONE tag, the outer VID 3995. The
     customer tag is not kept, and the inner is not translated to 3997 and kept either. The same
     with the provider port as a plain trunk or as `vlan-stacking provider-port`. NOT Q-in-Q.
   - Reverse (provider 3995 + any inner -> customer): the frame leaves with ONE tag, the wire VID
     2100, whatever the inner VID was (3997, 2100 or 3000). A provider's inner tag is not delivered.
   - The x930 page describes the combined entry as "both adds an outer-tag VID and translates the
     inner-tag VID between the wire-VID and the internal VID", which would give 3995,3997 forward.
     Measured: 3995 only. With the 3995/3997 reverse sent, 2100 out matches the documented reverse
     translation, but 3000 -> 2100 shows the inner VID is not checked.
2. O-2 form `vlan 2100 outer-vlan 3995`: forward ONE tag (3995); reverse 2100 for any inner.
   O-2 (measured 2026-09-30 on awplus_main-20260923-20) REPEATS on tomahawk_ie520-20260825-42.
   Behaviour (1) and (2) are indistinguishable on the wire.
3. (B) `default outer-vlan`: refused by the hardware layer on this build
   (`% Translation configuration of hardware failed`), on a trunk port of either member. It also
   needs trunk mode (`% VLAN translation only supported in trunk mode` on an access port).
4. The refused (B) line was stored on the backup member while the master refused it: a repeat of the
   2026-10-02 O-1 (refused flowcontrol landing on backups), here with a VLAN-translation command on
   the old build. Cleared with the `no` form on the master and verified by remote-diff.
5. Port-based QinQ (s1, control) works on this build: 3995,2100 forward, 2100 reverse.

